<Project>

  <!--
    The WebView2 package ships a WinForms wrapper and a WPF one, and the WPF one
    was built against WindowsBase 5.0 - which does not exist in .NET 8, whose own
    WindowsBase is 4.0.0.0. MSBuild cannot reconcile the two and every build
    reports MSB3277 "conflicts between different versions of WindowsBase that
    could not be resolved".

    Nothing here touches the WPF wrapper: the control is hosted in WinForms (see
    MainForm). So the reference is dropped rather than left as a permanent
    warning, because a build that always prints one warning is a build where the
    next, real warning goes unread.

    It has to happen here and not in a plain ItemGroup: @(Reference) is only
    populated from the package once ResolvePackageAssets has run, and the
    conflict is reported by ResolveAssemblyReferences - so this is the one window
    in between.
  -->
  <Target Name="DropWebView2WpfWrapper"
          AfterTargets="ResolvePackageAssets"
          BeforeTargets="ResolveAssemblyReferences">
    <ItemGroup>
      <Reference Remove="@(Reference)" Condition="'%(FileName)' == 'Microsoft.Web.WebView2.Wpf'" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

</Project>
